1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,370
There is an ocean floating in empty space.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,900
It holds 140 trillion times more water than Earth.

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:10,760
Twelve billion light-years away, a supermassive black hole consumes gas.

4
00:00:10,810 --> 00:00:15,000
This monster quasar releases energy equal to thousands of trillion suns.

5
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:18,520
Pause—how can liquid water survive near something so hot?

6
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:23,110
It isn't liquid, but vast water vapor stretched over hundreds of light-years.

7
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:27,440
The quasar's radiation bakes the surrounding dust, creating endless warm mist.

8
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:31,730
This water formed when the universe was only a tenth of its age.

9
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:36,510
It proves water was abundant almost immediately after the Big Bang.

10
00:00:36,550 --> 00:00:39,710
Which means in the ancient dark, there was already...
